AUTHORSHIP
----------
Curie is the work of SC Placeholder and Elah.

SC Placeholder proposed it and directed it. RELA (Relational Event and Amplitude Mathematics), the
framework Curie is written in, is his: he asked for Curie to become a quantum-computation sandbox
others could learn from, set what it is (a microscope, not a simulator), asked whether its mathematics
was actually correct (which produced the Qiskit and Cirq cross-checks), and decided its licence and
that it is published only when finished.

Elah planned each stage, checked every design by hand before it was built, verified each wave
(tests, off-specification values, the two cross-checks and the mutations that prove they can fail),
and wrote this repository's documentation and its wave bench.
